            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of all 3 sinuses of valsalva causing coronary insufficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>637-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492309349812</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 35-year-old woman presented with chest pain and easy fatigability. Transthoracic echocardiography demonstrated an unruptured aneurysm involving all 3 sinuses of Valsalva. Successful surgical repair was undertaken, without the need for aortic valve replacement or coronary artery bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
